  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Hederagenin 28-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl Ester and Neuropilin-2, as this compound is implicated in targeting WI-38 cells, which in turn are targets of multiple compounds. These compounds, including 3,5-Diethyltoluene and (6Ar)-1,10-Dimethoxy-6-Methyl-5,6,6A,7-Tetrahydro-4H-Dibenzo[De,G]Quinoline-2,9-Diol, are all known to interact with Neuropilin-2. The consistent presence of this compound as a target of multiple pathways indicates a possible role in modulating Neuropilin-2 activity. The scores assigned to these relationships are similar, suggesting a degree of confidence in the observed associations. However, the exact mechanism by which Hederagenin 28-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl Ester influences Neuropilin-2 remains unclear, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
